### Verify 2 — full auth-code flow through IAS (VS Code REST Client)
### Proves Step 1 (Entra -> IAS federation) AND Step 2 (App-2 audience).
### App-2 is a CONFIDENTIAL client (has a secret, no PKCE).
###
### Fill in the placeholders. NEVER commit the real client secret or an authorization code.

# iasHost: e.g. xxxxxxxxx.accounts.ondemand.com
@iasHost      = <ias-host>            
@clientId     = <app2-oauth-client-id>
@clientSecret = <app2-client-secret>  # store locally, do NOT commit
@redirectUri  = http://localhost:8080/callback
@scope        = openid
@authCode     = <paste-the-fresh-code-here>
@gateway      = https://<your-integration-suite-host>/swapi

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### STEP A (manual): open this URL in a browser.
### You should be redirected to the MICROSOFT login page (= federation works).
### After login the browser lands on http://localhost:8080/callback?code=...
### The page won't load - that's expected. Copy the value after ?code= into @authCode above.
###
### https://<ias-host>/oauth2/authorize?response_type=code&client_id=<app2-oauth-client-id>&redirect_uri=http://localhost:8080/callback&scope=openid
###
### IAS supports ONLY these scopes: openid, email, profile, offline_access, groups. No custom scopes.
### For a groups claim later (gateway authorization), use scope=openid%20groups.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------

### STEP B: exchange the authorization code for tokens
# @name token
POST https://{{iasHost}}/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code&code={{authCode}}&redirect_uri={{redirectUri}}&client_id={{clientId}}&client_secret={{clientSecret}}

### STEP C (optional): call the SWAPI MCP gateway with the IAS token (MCP initialize)
### Expect this to SUCCEED only after Step 3 (gateway External OIDC -> IAS) is deployed.
### Paste the access_token from Step B in place of <ias-access-token>.
POST {{gateway}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "initialize",
  "params": {
    "protocolVersion": "2024-11-05",
    "capabilities": {},
    "clientInfo": { "name": "resttest", "version": "1.0" }
  }
}
